case1=pagehead(root,'Campaign case study','From audience trust to <span class="serif highlight">600+ sales.</span>','A March 2026 affiliate campaign recognized by LearnerFlex — and what it says about clear communication and consistent execution.',True)+f'''<section class="section container case-layout"><article class="case-main"><h2>The context</h2><p>Digital product marketing is crowded. People are constantly exposed to new offers, and attention alone rarely converts into trust. My independent affiliate work centered on communicating value clearly, answering questions and maintaining audience engagement around educational digital products.</p><h2>The approach</h2><p>I focused on approachable explanations, follow-up conversations, consistent promotion and building relationships with people who needed to understand a product before making a decision.</p><p>This was an independent affiliate role rather than employment by LearnerFlex. No paid advertising spend, exact conversion rate or campaign attribution data is claimed here because the necessary records were not supplied.</p><div class="insight"><strong>Recognized outcome:</strong> More than 600 sales reported for March 2026 and No. 1 affiliate recognition on LearnerFlex, according to supplied award and social media screenshots.</div><figure class="case-figure"><img loading="lazy" src="{root}assets/media/award.webp" alt="LearnerFlex award graphic naming Muneerah top affiliate for March 2026"><figcaption>Award image supplied for this portfolio; issued as recognition for March 2026.</figcaption></figure><h2>What I learned</h2><p>Community-led marketing rewards consistent, clear communication. I want to apply those same skills in structured marketing and customer experience teams, with better analytics, transparent reporting and long-term customer relationships.</p><p>{a(root,'evidence/','View related evidence <span class="arr">↗</span>','btn btn-ghost')}</p></article><aside class="case-aside"><dl><dt>Project</dt><dd>Affiliate marketing campaign</dd><dt>Platform</dt><dd>LearnerFlex</dd><dt>Period</dt><dd>March 2026 recognition</dd><dt>Responsibilities</dt><dd>Promotion, audience engagement, communication and follow-up</dd><dt>Reported outcome</dt><dd>600+ sales / #1 affiliate ranking</dd><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Award graphic, dashboard, X screenshot</dd></dl></aside></section>'''
shell('work/learnerflex/','LearnerFlex Campaign','Case study of Muneerah’s March 2026 #1 LearnerFlex affiliate recognition and more than 600 reported sales.',case1,active='work/')

case2=pagehead(root,'Community case study','A community is built <span class="serif highlight">one person at a time.</span>','Creating supportive spaces for learners, maintaining engagement and making questions easy to ask.',True)+f'''<section class="section container case-layout"><article class="case-main"><h2>The context</h2><p>Newcomers to online business and digital learning often need a welcoming place to ask questions and understand their next step. I organized and supported Telegram and WhatsApp groups aimed at sharing practical information and peer guidance.</p><h2>The approach</h2><p>My day-to-day involvement included community announcements, onboarding-style explanations, keeping members informed, responding to common questions and helping maintain consistent participation.</p><p>Multiple screenshots show growth across different communities, including an online survey-focused Telegram group of 1,261 members and a course channel with 2,251 subscribers. These are separate snapshots, not a combined unique-audience count.</p><div class="insight"><strong>Community milestone:</strong> Screenshot-based evidence includes a Telegram group with 1,261 members and another course channel at 2,251 subscribers. Exact ownership and growth attribution should be confirmed before external publication.</div><figure class="case-figure"><img loading="lazy" src="{root}assets/media/community-survey.webp" alt="Telegram community screenshot displaying 1,261 members"><figcaption>A community snapshot supplied for this portfolio; counts reflect the moment the screenshot was taken.</figcaption></figure><h2>What transfers into a professional team</h2><p>The experience is relevant to community operations, Telegram moderation, welcome flows, member communication and customer-facing support. I have not represented this as previous employment at a crypto exchange or as professional Discord moderation experience.</p></article><aside class="case-aside"><dl><dt>Area</dt><dd>Community growth & engagement</dd><dt>Channels</dt><dd>Telegram, WhatsApp</dd><dt>Period</dt><dd>2025–2026 (approx.)</dd><dt>Shown milestone</dt><dd>1,261 members / 2,251 subscribers</dd><dt>Work included</dt><dd>Member communication, engagement and educational guidance</dd><dt>Next goal</dt><dd>Structured community or customer experience teams</dd></dl></aside></section>'''
